==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|lahs}}, from {{inh|de|goh|lahs}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*lahs}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*lahsaz}}.{{dercat|de|ine-pro}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/laks/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Lachs.OGG}}
* {{homophones|de|Lacks|lax}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m}}

# [[salmon]], [[lax]]/[[lox]]
# [[longissimus]] dorsi (core muscle, long back extensor muscle) of the back of slaughtered animals, especially pigs (Schweinelachs or Lachsfleisch), calves (Kalbslachs), and lambs (Lammlachs); part of the rib or chop cuts.

